.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PROC_TERMINATE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm proc_terminate
.Nd terminate a process and all its threads
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn proc_terminate proc code
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
terminates the target process and every thread it owns, stores
.Fa code
for
.Xr proc_wait 2 ,
and runs the same one-shot teardown as
.Xr exit 2 :
scheme names owned by the process are released, pending requests fail, the address space and
handle table are torn down and waiters are woken.
A runnable thread of the target stops before it can run user code again; a thread blocked in a
syscall exits at its next scheduling point.
.Pp
This is the authorized termination primitive for service supervision (contract C16).
The caller must hold the
.Dv SIGNAL
right on the process handle; a handle duplicated without it fails with
.Er EPERM .
Terminating the calling process behaves like
.Xr exit 2 .
.Pp
A second call on a terminal process fails with
.Er ESRCH ;
the exit code and the reap are observed once, through
.Xr proc_wait 2 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Zero on success; a negative
.Va errno
on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa proc
is not a valid process handle.
.It Er EPERM
The handle lacks the
.Dv SIGNAL
right.
.It Er ESRCH
The target process is already terminal.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr exit 2 ,
.Xr proc_create 2 ,
.Xr proc_wait 2 ,
.Xr thread_exit 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
